WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.096
Welcome to EventClaim, the Cursor Community portal for distributing partner credits at events.

2
00:00:06.096 --> 00:00:12.744
Before you run an event, complete the most important step: set up Luma and EmailJS in Settings.

3
00:00:12.744 --> 00:00:24.000
Open the Setup guide for step-by-step instructions. Configure your Luma API key to sync checked-in guests, then connect EmailJS so claim emails can be sent.

4
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:34.080
Save your Luma and EmailJS values here. They stay encrypted in this browser only. Once configured, you are ready to create events.

5
00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:41.352
The dashboard gives an overview across all events — attendees, coupons, emails sent, and claim rate.

6
00:00:41.352 --> 00:00:47.232
Open Events to browse meetups or create a new one with a name, date, and venue details.

7
00:00:47.232 --> 00:00:52.488
Inside an event, you see live stats and shortcuts for the full coupon workflow.

8
00:00:52.488 --> 00:01:02.424
Import checked-in guests from a Luma CSV export, then upload coupon links. The portal pairs available credits with attendees automatically.

9
00:01:02.424 --> 00:01:10.560
On Attendees, search, filter, and send or resend claim emails. Each guest gets a unique claim link.

10
00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:16.872
Partner Offers lets you manage coupon types, track available links, and see what has been granted.

11
00:01:16.872 --> 00:01:22.728
Audit Logs record admin activity so you can review imports, emails, and claims.

12
00:01:22.728 --> 00:01:34.680
That is EventClaim. Set up Luma and EmailJS first, then create an event, import guests, send claims, and track redemptions. Thanks for watching.
